[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b13: the angular scale of the structure
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   The comet-side analysis (steps 12-16) found the clock-channel
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   anomaly is a broad ~60-70 deg patch, not a point.  This step
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   measures the angular scale of the detached-TNO cluster on the
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   same footing, so the two populations can be compared.
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   P1  Cap-radius significance profile: in-cap counts vs the
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   conditioned null for caps 20-120 deg.  The radius of peak
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   significance is the detection-optimal angular scale.
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   P2  Intrinsic width: refit the uniform + von-Mises mixture;
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   the cluster component's kappa -> sigma_cluster = 1/sqrt(k).
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   Bootstrap CI on both f and sigma.
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   P3  Direction wandering: bootstrap the cluster-centre estimate
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   -- does the recovered direction wander like the comet
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   patch's (~24-55 deg between catalogues)?
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   P4  3-D check: the same cap profile on perihelion vectors in
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   3-D (angular distance from the 3-D axis), verifying the
[2026-09-20 10:42:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 025]   scale is not an ecliptic-projection artifact.
